message: "If you use this testbed, corpus or the rated artefacts, please cite both the software release and the paper."
type: software
title: "Zero-Trust SOAR Remediation Testbed: synthetic Teleport database-access corpus, LLM remediation artefacts and blind ratings"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
authors:
  - given-names: Johannes Haposan
    family-names: Napitupulu
    affiliation: "Monash University"
  - given-names: Muhamad Erza
    family-names: Aminanto
    affiliation: "Monash University"
url: "https://github.com/haposan06/zt-soar-remediation-testbed"
repository-code: "https://github.com/haposan06/zt-soar-remediation-testbed"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A fully local zero-trust database-access testbed (Teleport 17 in front of
  PostgreSQL 16) that emits genuine Teleport audit logs from scripted benign
  and malicious sessions, eleven YARA-L 2.0 detection rules and their Python
  evaluator, the resulting 18 alerts, a generation harness that asks Gemini
  3.1 Pro, Claude Opus 4.6 and a template baseline for remediation scripts,
  the 126 resulting artefacts, a blind two-rater coding of every artefact and
  the analysis code that reproduces the reported statistics. All data is
  synthetic.
keywords:
  - zero trust
  - SOAR
  - security orchestration
  - generative AI
  - large language models
  - incident response
  - remediation
  - Teleport
  - PostgreSQL
  - YARA-L
  - audit logs
  - testbed
  - reproducibility
